th $m=3.022\\, 1$ and the coordinates of our point $(2, 0.497\\, 0)$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 0.4970 &= 3.0221(x - 2) \\\\\ny - 0.4970 &= 3.0221x - 6.0442 \\\\\ny &= 3.0221x - 5.5472\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, rounding the coefficients to one decimal place, we find that the approximate normal line is given by\n\n$$\ny = 3.0x - 5.5\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186166484 1074 "Evaluating $f(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a calculator, we get\n\n$$\ny = f(2) = \\dfrac{\\ln((2)^2+8)}{(2)^2+1} \\approx 0.497\\, 0\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places.\n\nThe slope of the normal line is the negative reciprocal of the derivative of $f(x)$ at $x=2$.\n\nWe bring up the derivative option on most calculators in one of the following ways:\n\n- Using the $\\bbox[2px, border: 2px solid gray]{\\color{gray}\\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\bbox[gray]{\\phantom{00}}\\,}$ button. You may need to press the $\\bbox[2px, border: 2px solid gray]{\\color{gray}\\,2\\text{nd}\\,}$ (or $\\bbox[2px, border: 2px solid gray]{\\color{gray}\\,\\text{shift}\\,}$) button first.\n- Press the $\\bbox[2px, border: 2px solid gray]{\\color{gray}\\,\\text{math}\\,}$ (or $\\bbox[2px, border: 2px solid gray]{\\color{gray}\\,\\text{calc}\\,}$) button and choose the derivative option. Note that this might be called $\\bbox[2px, border: 2px solid gray]{\\color{gray}\\,\\text{nDeriv}\\,}$ or similar.\n\nEvaluating the derivative using a calculator, we obtain\n\n$$\nf'(2) = \\left. \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} \\left(\\dfrac{\\ln(x^2+8)}{x^2+1} \\right) \\right|_{x=2} \\approx -0.330\\, 9\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the normal is\n\n$$\nm = -\\dfrac{1}{f'(2)} = -\\dfrac{1}{-0.330\\, 9} = 3.022\\, 1\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=3.022\\, 1$ and the coordinates of our point $(2, 0.497\\, 0)$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 0.4970 &= 3.02